
=== (a) first-order field of h(x)=p+(x-p)/(1+sigma(x-p)) in the modular frame ===
**FAIL** zeta*w(y-y_p) identity, zeta=sigma*beta_I(p), w(u)=-4 sinh^2(u/2)  (rel.err 6.66e-03)
PASS Theorem A zeta = a s/(a+L):  35/153 == 35/153

=== (b) Schwarzian of a C^1 piecewise-Moebius map ===
PASS right-compression jump = -2 sigma  (-0.740000 vs -0.740000)
PASS left-compression  jump = -2 sigma  (-0.740000 vs -0.740000)
PASS R(s1) o R(s2) == R(s1+s2) exactly
PASS L(s1) o R(s2) == M_{-s1} o R(s1+s2) (global Moebius x single corner)
PASS ...and its Schwarzian jump = -2(s1+s2)  (-1.960000)
PASS R(s2) o L(s1) has the same Schwarzian jump (-1.960000)

=== (b) VWZ Protocols 1(A), 1(B), 2, 3 ===
PASS 1(B) identity 2c/(b(b+c)) + 2d/((b+c)(b+c+d)) = 2(c+d)/(b(b+c+d))  [344/365]
PASS Protocol 1(B) point map == Protocol 1(A) point map LITERALLY (max|diff| = 2.22e-16)
PASS Protocol 2: two corners, jump at p2 = -2*0.757895 (-1.515789)
PASS Protocol 2: jump at p3 = -2*0.661499 (-1.322997)
PASS sigma_1 = 2a/(b(a+b)) = 96/235
PASS sigma_2 = 2d/(c(c+d)) = 256/387
PASS Protocol 3 composite == (global Moebius) o R(sigma_1+sigma_2) at p3 (max|diff| 8.88e-16)
      (it is NOT literally equal to the single compression: max|diff| = 0.6828)
PASS zeta_eff = (s1+s2)(a+b)(c+d)/(a+b+c+d) = 24328/26235

=== (d) amplification lemma ===
PASS beta_I(p)/beta_Istep(p) = 1 + z', z' = cross ratio = ac/(b(a+b+c))  (0/20000 bad)

=== (e) L->R Petz chain: zeta_k^(I), e^{Delta_k}, separation inequality ===
PASS e^{Delta_k}=(1+u_k)(1+v_k), zeta_k^(I)=2r(1+v)/((1+r)(e^D-1)), (e^D-1)zeta>=2r/(1+r)  (0 bad)
      min over 20000 random chains of (e^D-1)zeta / (2r/(1+r)) = 1.000157  (>=1, =1+v_k)
      scan: smallest e^{Delta_k} compatible with zeta_k,zeta_{k+1} <= eps
        eps=0.30  min e^{Delta} = 1.132   (eps * min e^{Delta} = 0.3397)
        eps=0.10  min e^{Delta} = 1.303   (eps * min e^{Delta} = 0.1303)
        eps=0.03  min e^{Delta} = 1.557   (eps * min e^{Delta} = 0.0467)
        eps=0.01  min e^{Delta} = 2.88   (eps * min e^{Delta} = 0.0288)

